§ `s 8 -- Census years (c049 2026, k047 2031, d048 2032)`

#ASSERT `Is a Census taken in the year` 2026 FALSE
#ASSERT `Is a Census taken in the year` 2031 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is a Census taken in the year` 2032 FALSE
#ASSERT `Is a Census taken in the year` 2033 TRUE

§ `ss 10, 11 -- was I asked in a way the Act allows`

#ASSERT `Was I asked in a way the Act allows` `Chloe on Census night under the Census instrument (c049)`
#ASSERT NOT `Was I asked in a way the Act allows` `Jake at his sister's, outside the instrument's class (k047)`
#ASSERT NOT `Was I asked in a way the Act allows` `Jarrah sent the survey as if under the Census instrument (d048)`
#ASSERT `Was I asked in a way the Act allows` `Jarrah asked by email to complete the survey (d048)`

#ASSERT `Was I validly directed` `Chloe 20 days after a direction giving 14 days (c049)`
#ASSERT NOT `Was I validly directed` `Jake directed with only 7 days (k047)`
#ASSERT NOT `Was I validly directed` `Jake directed without the s 14 warning (k047)`

§ `Must I fill this in`

#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Chloe on Census night under the Census instrument (c049)` EQUALS `I am required by the Census instrument, but not answering is not itself an offence`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Liam asked at the door by a collector (c049)` EQUALS `I am only requested, and not answering is not an offence`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Chloe 20 days after a direction giving 14 days (c049)` EQUALS `I am directed, and not complying once the period runs is an offence (s 14)`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Jake at his sister's, outside the instrument's class (k047)` EQUALS `I have not been validly asked, so nothing is required of me`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Jake directed with only 7 days (k047)` EQUALS `the notice falls short of s 10(4)-(5) or 11(2)-(3), so on this encoding not complying is not an offence`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Jake directed without the s 14 warning (k047)` EQUALS `the notice falls short of s 10(4)-(5) or 11(2)-(3), so on this encoding not complying is not an offence`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Jake 35 days after a direction giving 21 days (k047)` EQUALS `I am directed, and not complying once the period runs is an offence (s 14)`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Jarrah sent the survey as if under the Census instrument (d048)` EQUALS `I have not been validly asked, so nothing is required of me`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Jarrah asked by email to complete the survey (d048)` EQUALS `I am only requested, and not answering is not an offence`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Jarrah 40 days after a direction giving 28 days (d048)` EQUALS `I am directed, and not complying once the period runs is an offence (s 14)`
#ASSERT `Must I fill this in` `Nobody asked (d048)` EQUALS `I have not been validly asked, so nothing is required of me`

§ `s 14 -- not answering`

#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed an offence by not answering` `Chloe on Census night under the Census instrument (c049)`
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by not answering` `Chloe 20 days after a direction giving 14 days (c049)`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed an offence by not answering` `Chloe 10 days after the direction (c049)`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed an offence by not answering` `Chloe after the direction, having complied (c049)`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed an offence by not answering` `Chloe after the direction, leaving only religion blank (c049)`
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by not answering` `Jake 35 days after a direction giving 21 days (k047)`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed an offence by not answering` `Jarrah asked by email to complete the survey (d048)`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed an offence by not answering` `Jarrah exactly at the end of its 28 days (d048)`

#ASSERT `Is this question optional` `my religious beliefs`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this question optional` `any other matter`

#ASSERT `How many daily offences have I committed` `Chloe 20 days after a direction giving 14 days (c049)` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `How many daily offences have I committed` `Jake 35 days after a direction giving 21 days (k047)` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `How many daily offences have I committed` `Jarrah 40 days after a direction giving 28 days (d048)` EQUALS 12

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for not answering in penalty units` `Jake 35 days after a direction giving 21 days (k047)` EQUALS 14

-- the value of a penalty unit is an input; 100 is hypothetical, not read from any deposit
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for not answering in dollars` `Jarrah 40 days after a direction giving 28 days (d048)` 100 EQUALS 1200

§ `s 15 -- answering falsely`

#ASSERT `Is my false answer an offence` `Chloe on Census night under the Census instrument (c049)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my false answer an offence` `Chloe on Census night under the Census instrument (c049)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my false answer an offence` `Liam asked at the door by a collector (c049)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my false answer an offence` `Nobody asked (d048)` TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 14, 15, 19, 20 -- maximum penalties`

#ASSERT `What is the most that can be fined in penalty units` `my not complying with a direction (s 14)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be fined in penalty units` `my false or misleading answer (s 15)` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be fined in penalty units` `an officer passing on what I gave, on indictment (s 19)` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be fined in penalty units` `an officer passing on what I gave, heard summarily (s 19, s 20(3))` EQUALS 20

#ASSERT `What is the longest imprisonment in months` `an officer passing on what I gave, on indictment (s 19)` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `What is the longest imprisonment in months` `an officer passing on what I gave, heard summarily (s 19, s 20(3))` EQUALS 12

